-- =====================================================================
-- Royal Hotel (royalhotel.com) - backup of the royalhotel database: tables, keys, rules and data
-- (23 rooms, 100 users, about 2,400 bookings over 12 months back and 3 months ahead, about 500 sample reviews).
-- Passwords are stored as hashes.
-- RolePortals: the port of each role (Customer 5243, Staff 5244, Housekeeper 5245, Finance 5246, Admin 5247,
-- Super Admin 5248), fixed in the code and restored by the site on every start; Users.Role is a foreign key to it.
-- Stay dates, birthdays and shift days are DATE columns; CHECK constraints and UNIQUE indexes: see 02_schema.sql.
-- HotelBookings.CancelReason says why a booking was cancelled (PaymentTimeout: booked online but no payment
-- method chosen within 30 minutes, so the site cancelled it; NoShow: the guest never came, the payment is kept - no refund).
-- HotelBookings.SpecialRequest is the guest's note for the hotel (max 500 characters, empty when none).
-- RoomReviews: guest reviews (1-5 stars), one per checked-out stay; IsHidden = taken down by an admin.
-- AuditLogs: who did what and when (append-only).
-- The old unused Promotions table is gone.
-- Restore (replaces the tables of the royalhotel database). The file is UTF-8 with Thai text: Windows PowerShell
-- must read and send it as UTF-8, otherwise every Thai letter arrives as "?":
--   $OutputEncoding = [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false)
--   Get-Content -Raw -Encoding UTF8 Database\03_royalhotel_dump.sql | & "C:\Program Files\MySQL\MySQL Server 26.7\bin\mysql.exe" -u royalhotel_app -p royalhotel
-- (cmd.exe: "C:\Program Files\MySQL\MySQL Server 26.7\bin\mysql.exe" -u royalhotel_app -p royalhotel < Database\03_royalhotel_dump.sql)
-- Demo accounts: see README.md
-- User #5 is a real member of the live site: in this file its name, e-mail, phone, birthday and password
-- are sample values (log in as sample.member@example.org / demo1234).
-- =====================================================================

